      text: "Clemency is leniency of a superior in fixing the punishment of an inferior; and this is something distinct from meekness, which moderates anger. For clemency does not concern the passion of anger, but the very act of punishment, which it mitigates. The clement man, when he holds the rod, is not slow to use it; he is slow to use the full weight of it. He measures the blow to the offender, not to his own heart.",
