      text: "In determining the gravity of theft, we must consider not only the quantity of the thing stolen, but also the condition of the thief and of the one from whom it is taken. For one who steals from necessity, being driven by hunger, is not in the same case as one who steals from greed; nor is one who has been raised in the discipline of justice in the same case as one who has known no order from his youth. The judge who weighs the act without weighing the life weighs unjustly, even when his arithmetic is correct.",
